{% extends "common/layout.html.twig" %}

{% block body %}

  <h1>The LEAGUE ! New format</h3>

  <p>Time to try a new format and experience another system for our League.</p>
  <p>We keep the same backbone : <b>every registered player is expected to play (at least) 5 games during the 10-weeks round</b>.</p>
  <p>Here is a recap of how the new format works : </p>
  <ul>
    <li>No more divisions, but only <b>one standings table</b> with all the players</li>
    <li>All the registered players are listed in *the entry list*, sorted by ratings (our Stegen 6-months average rating)</li>
    <li><b>Based on the entry list</b>, every player can play matches against the 6 players ranked above her/him, and the 6 ranked below her/him (except for the top2 and bottom2 who can challenge 9 players above/below). <b>The entry list prevails for the entire round.</b></li>
    <li>All the players receive at the beginning of the round the list of players (+ phone numbers) who can be contacted, based on their position in the entry list</li>
    <li>Match format will be most of the time a 1-hour match with as many games played as possible. But of course as usual : <i>pick the format you want as long as both you and your opponent agree on it</i> ! </li>
    <li>in the standings table, the point system will be : Win=3pts, Tie=2pts, Loss=1pt. And one extra point for each win against a player with a higher rank in the entry list ;-)</li>
    <li>You can play more than 5 games if you want/can, but only your 5 best results are counted in the table</li>
  </ul>
  <br>

  <p>The goal to have a more flexible format that allows anyone to have opportunities to play fun matches against players of similar levels. And to avoid W/Os :)</p>
  <p>Some of you may play 10 matches, some only a couple. Everybody can set his/her own goals : being a finisher (playing 5 games), trying to be as high as possible in the standings table, meeting the most opponents, etc.</p>

